# Human-reviewed class notes. VAs are ArcCore 1.170.0 unslid addresses.
NOTES={
'ArcAIInferenceConfiguration':('The initializer engages an inline configuration, stores maxTokens as int32 at +8 and truncates streamAfterEveryNTokens to signed int16 at +0xc (0x443a318). Getters require the engagement byte at +0x10; an empty configuration traps rather than returning defaults (0x443a3d4, 0x443a3e8). The mutable accessor returns interior storage (0x443a2fc); the aggregate getter copies the optional (0x443a3fc).','No callback is installed here. ArcAIService consumes this configuration through its streaming adapter at 0x43d7a5c → 0x443a40c. There is no persistence operation in these IMPs.','Arc-specific value adapter; either backend needs the Arc ABI and integer narrowing behavior. No CEF API equivalence is established.','Confirm overflow/negative token handling at the service boundary, and whether app callers rely on the signed 16-bit truncation.'),
'ArcAIInferenceModel':('This is an engaged optional value, not the loaded model itself. init:directory: writes the model discriminator and converts the directory string (0x4439f8c); initWithAIInferenceModel: copies native string storage (0x443a094). modelType and directory check engagement (0x443a13c, 0x443a150); destruction frees an allocated string only while engaged (0x43ded20).','The aggregate getter copies the model descriptor (0x443a180). ArcAIService loadInferenceModel and streamInference consume it through the adapter 0x443a21c (callers 0x43d77b0, 0x43d7a5c). No model file is opened by the inspected model IMPs.','Arc-specific descriptor; backend model loading lives beyond this class. CEF alone does not specify Arc model format.','Recover modelType enum meanings and validation rules in the loader; distinguish descriptor lifetime from loaded resource lifetime.'),
'ArcAIService':('initWithAIService: stores an engaged shared native handle, incrementing its control count (0x4439e68). ai_service copies the optional handle and increments its count (0x43df53c); .cxx_destruct releases it (0x43df69c). All service operations are in the Extensions category, distinct from the four base declarations.','Extensions marshal strings, vectors and ObjC callback objects into native operations. Streaming has separate partial-result and completion adapters, and returns the native token (0x43d7a5c → 0x43310bc → 0x429fa38). The latter installs ai.mojom.AIStreamedInferenceListener and uses ai.mojom.AIService; its early unavailable branch invokes completion and returns zero (0x429fa38). Other callback error shapes, cancellation and delivery queues remain unresolved.','Arc-specific service and Mojo protocol. Chrome or CEF hosting still needs a compatible service boundary; this analysis does not include libaperitif execution or prove it implements these endpoints.','Recover callback adapter vtables and exact result/error/token contracts for every operation; determine which service implementation and library version the app actually supplies.'),
'ArcAIServiceConfiguration':('init:displayName:libraryPath:libraryVersion:appEnvironment:fullAppVersion:maxRetries:timeout:error: rejects type -1 with NSError domain company.thebrowser.Arc, code 2 and Invalidtype text, writing the supplied error pointer (0x43dcbdc). It uses libraryPath.path, converts five strings, narrows maxRetries to a signed byte at +0x88 and stores a double at +0x90. Optional engagement is +0x98.','nativeAIServiceConfig copies an engaged configuration and setNativeAIServiceConfig: implements engaged/empty assignment (0x43dd120, 0x43dd184); destruction calls 0x42a3344 only while engaged (0x43dd3a0). No callback registration or library loading happens in these configuration IMPs. The timeout getter has a decompiler signature defect; raw instructions load d0 from +0x90 after the engagement check (0x43dd10c).','Arc-specific configuration ABI including narrowing and error behavior; strings describe external service deployment, without proving any particular library identity.','Determine valid service type values, whether nil error pointers are ever used on the rejection path, and allowed retry/timeout ranges.'),
'ArcAnnotatedVisit':('The ObjC object owns optional unique storage: init allocates a 0x150-byte flat record and sets task/root/parent IDs to -1 (0x43fed80); native-copy init uses 0x4336aac (0x43fee60); destruction calls 0x4336e98 then frees it (0x4400f18). Setters mutate this local record, with no demonstrated database write. Empty getters have individual defaults, including current NSDate for visitTime (0x43ff064).','visitTime stores Unix seconds through NSDate rather than a direct base::Time field (0x43ffac0). Redirect chains wrap ArcRedirectEntry (0x43ff0fc); categories wrap ArcVisitCategory (0x43ff438). Setters rebuild corresponding vectors (0x43ffb30, 0x44001d0, 0x4400620). Stock history::AnnotatedVisit at Chromium components/history/core/browser/history_types.h:1029 is a source-backed domain comparison, not an established layout identity.','Chrome history integration is plausible, but this flat Arc record is a separate serialization boundary. A CEF route would need to supply the rich annotation, redirect and provenance contract independently; completeness is unproven.','Follow the history producer/consumer and 0x4336aac before mapping flat fields to upstream history structs; validate empty-state and enum behavior against app use.'),
'ArcAutocompleteResult':('init:perProviderMatches: stores two ObjC collections at +8 and +0x10 after NSObject init (0x43df204). Accessors return those slots (0x43dd450, 0x420b5f8); destruction clears both (0x43dd5a4). It does not compute or merge matches.','No delegate registration occurs in this class. The exact element classes, collection mutability and copy-versus-retain policy are not fully established because retain/release fixups obscure the stores (0x43df204). It is distinct from the array constructed by autocomplete completion at 0x43eceb0.','A result container can be backend independent. Matching/ranking/provider behavior must be obtained from the producer; its class name does not prove Chrome or CEF equivalence.','Find the producer of this combined/per-provider result and actual app consumers; establish collection ownership and ordering.'),
'ArcBrowserContextAttributes':('The native attributes value begins at +0x10; +8 caches an ArcColor object. Initialization delegates to native assignment at 0x441e0a0 (0x443afd0). directoryBasename and userVisibleName convert native strings (0x443ab84, 0x443aba8). userColor lazily constructs and caches ArcColor from native color storage at +0x40 (0x443b028).','Aggregate getter copies strings and color (0x443b07c); aggregate setter calls 0x441e0a0 (0x443b0f4). Destruction frees native strings and clears cached color (0x443b100). The setter only passes self+0x10 to 0x441e0a0, which updates native strings/color without touching the cached ObjC slot at self+8; an already-created userColor wrapper therefore remains unchanged along this assignment path (0x443b0f4, 0x441e0a0, 0x443b028). No disk operation is shown.','Arc profile presentation data. Either hosting route can marshal values, but profile identity/persistence and cached-color invalidation must match the engine contract.','Does the app use the stale cached-color path after native reassignment, and what owns/updates the persisted profile attributes?'),
'ArcBrowserContextAutocomplete':('initWithAutocompleteController: moves a pointer from the supplied controller owner and nulls that source (0x43ecb50); destruction disposes the controller using 0x42c33cc (0x43ece68). A request converts nil text to an empty string, stores a callback adapter and forwards cursor/prevent-inline arguments (0x43ecc2c → 0x42c35e4).','0x42c35e4 replaces the saved callback, constructs an input with a literal 4 and starts a controller via 0x20cd850. Completion builds an NSArray of ArcAutocompleteMatch and invokes the captured block with an additional argument (0x43eceb0). stop checks controller state, invokes a virtual stop-like operation, and clears callback storage (0x43ece08). Chromium components/omnibox/browser/autocomplete_controller.cc:631 and :797 provide a source-backed Start/Stop hypothesis; exact function identity remains unproven.','A Chrome omnibox service is strongly suggested by input/controller behavior; CEF replacement needs explicit provider/ranking semantics, not only URL navigation. No complete API exclusion is claimed.','Identify the completion additional argument, cancellation/supersession rules, controller lifetime, and callback thread; verify cursor narrowing to int in 0x42c35e4.'),
'ArcBrowserContextID':('initWithBrowserContextID: copies a basename string and native discriminator into optional storage (0x43ed360). isIncognito returns discriminator == 1 after an engagement check (0x43ed454); directoryBasename converts the string (0x43ed470). id returns an aggregate copy rather than a unique numeric identifier (0x43ed4a0).','Destruction frees heap string storage only for an engaged value (0x43ed510); construction clears engagement (0x43ed538). No profile creation, directory traversal or callback registration is present in these IMPs.','Backend-independent Arc profile identity wrapper; mapping incognito identities to real browser contexts requires external service policy.','Determine valid discriminator values and basename canonicalization; verify whether app compares native IDs or only exposed strings/flags.'),
'ArcColor':('The four-byte field is at +8. r/g/b/a return successive bytes +8/+9/+0xa/+0xb (0x40b1230, 0x43ecb04, 0x43ecb0c, 0x440c5a4); the r IMP is also used for a Boolean in ArcWebLoginDialog, so its Ghidra name/type is not authoritative. Init category initWithR:g:b:a: packs the bytes and invokes initWithColor: (0x4401b58).','initWithColor: copies the four bytes (0x443b164); color uses the hidden aggregate return destination, obscured by Ghidra, and setColor: copies four bytes (0x443b1b0, 0x443b1bc; raw prefix evidence). Both C++ lifecycle declarations alias the same return-only IMP 0x15ac0. No callback or persistence occurs in these bodies.','A four-byte Arc value ABI. Do not map its memory byte order to a Chromium SkColor integer without checking caller packing.','Validate endianness and alpha/premultiplication semantics at the native conversion boundary; preserve hidden return calling convention.'),
'ArcCommandBarRankingEvaluation':('An optional evaluation holds a metrics vector, count at +0x20 and duration integer at +0x24. Initializer enumerates dictionary keys, converts keys and double values, then stores counts (0x4433ba8). metrics reconstructs an NSMutableDictionary with NSNumber double values (0x4434190).','mutableCommandBarRankingEvaluation returns interior storage only if engaged (0x442c260). Aggregate copy uses 0x4434430; .cxx_destruct frees vector string allocations (0x4434298, 0x4434380). No ranking execution, callback scheduling or persistence occurs here.','Arc AI evaluation DTO. Independent of Chromium hosting, but dictionary conversion and numeric types are part of the interface.','Check duplicate metric keys, metrics ordering assumptions and duration/count narrowing; identify how service callbacks populate this value.'),
'ArcCommandBarRankingExample':('An engaged optional example owns input and candidate-vector state; selectedIndex is int32 at +0x38 (0x4433658). init:candidates:selectedIndex: converts the input, enumerates candidates into native structures, and stores the index (0x4433124); no bounds check on selectedIndex was established.','Extensions category input and candidates copy the native example and construct ArcCommandBarRankingInput/ArcCommandBarRankingCandidate wrappers (0x4401ca0, 0x4401f34). Aggregate copies use 0x43dad44 (0x4433528, 0x443366c); destruction frees nested state (0x4433768). These are not training operations.','Arc ranking example DTO; both routes need conversion behavior, while model evaluation/training belongs to ArcAIService (0x43d9ab8, 0x43d9fd4).','Resolve candidate ordering and selectedIndex validation; verify independent ownership of returned input/candidate wrappers.'),
'ArcContentConversionService':('init allocates a shared ContentConversionServiceImpl and constructs it at 0x42a6200 (0x43dd9d4). initWithImpl: stores a shared native implementation (0x43dd794); destruction releases its control block (0x43de5e8). initialize converts libraryPath.path plus identity/version/environment strings and installs a callback adapter (0x43ddb74).','HTML conversion marshals text, optional URL, enum/options, Boolean flags and a vector built from ArcMetaTagSelector kind/value before calling 0x42a75b4 (0x43de074). That backend retains completion by request ID, has an unavailable early completion branch, and binds content_conversion.mojom.ContentConversionService (0x42a75b4). Conversion algorithm/library contents and completion queue are not recovered.','Arc service protocol, not proof of stock Chromium HTML-to-Markdown behavior. CEF can host a separate service, but matching conversion and metadata policies remains required.','Recover callback result/error shape, URL transform and enum validation; determine library initialization failure behavior and helper/service ownership.'),
'ArcContextMenuElementInfo':('Initialization stores an optional shared native context record (0x443f0a0); destruction releases it (0x43df69c). x/y read native int32 at +4/+8 through the handle (0x443f1c4, 0x443f1dc); URL and text accessors convert native values, including selection text at +0x1c0 (0x443f404). Most access requires engagement.','dictionarySuggestions constructs a new array of native UTF-16 strings (0x443f654). inputType maps native enum 15..23 through table 0xc9d8198, returns zero when optional input type is absent and five outside that range (0x443f844). nodeType maps native 0..6 using 0xc9d81a8, trapping outside it (0x443f88c). These are metadata adapters; no menu is displayed here.','Context-menu data can be adapted by either route, but coordinate space, enum translation and top/subframe distinctions require explicit mapping. Stock Blink fields are domain context only, not proven struct identity.','Establish coordinate units and enum names; verify suggestion lifetime and all supported native node/input kinds.'),
'ArcDisplayNameOrOrigin':('The record holds a native UTF-16 string plus an isOrigin byte at +0x20. Initialization copies native string state (0x443b898), nameOrOrigin converts it through 0x1d9fb90 (0x441cefc), and isOrigin directly loads the flag (0x4081f00).','Aggregate getter copies the string and flag; setter assigns both (0x443b948, 0x443b998). Destruction frees long-string storage (0x443ba1c). There is no demonstrated origin parsing, formatting policy, delegate or persistence operation in this class.','Backend-independent presentation DTO; origin/security policy must be supplied by its producer.','Find who chooses display-name versus origin and whether strings are already escaped/localized.'),
'ArcExtensionInfo':('An optional inline extension snapshot contains name/ID/description/version/keyword strings, URL, permissions, icon and scalar flags. Default init engages a default native record (0x442f174); native-copy init uses 0x4334f1c (0x442f218); destructor uses 0x4334d2c (0x442f528). Getters generally trap if empty.','permissions constructs an array of strings (0x442f330); icon returns nil for empty image state or converts it (0x442f3f0). enabled, hasAction and fromWebstore are stored flags (0x442f444, 0x442f458, 0x442f4cc). None of these IMPs installs, enables or executes an extension.','Chrome extension data needs an actual extension-service producer for a full replacement. The DTO alone is portable; compatibility of extension execution under a CEF route remains outside this evidence.','Find snapshot refresh points, permission text localization, icon representation and extension-service dependencies.'),
'ArcExtensionToolbarAction':('Initialization copies the native toolbar-action record via 0x441e6d8 (0x443bc48). id is a converted native byte string (0x43e632c), accessibleName/tooltipText are converted UTF-16 (0x443bca0, 0x443bcc4), and icon is nil when the image is absent (0x443bce8).','pinnedPosition boxes a present optional integer and returns nil when absent (0x443bd08); enabled reads +0x68 (0x4243428). Aggregate assignment and lifecycle call native helpers (0x443bd4c, 0x443bd58, 0x443bd60). This object does not invoke a toolbar action or persist pinning.','Arc snapshot of Chrome-extension toolbar state; CEF feasibility depends on the producer/action API, not these getters.','Confirm pinning-index meaning and absence semantics, snapshot ownership, and refresh after extension action changes.'),
'ArcGPULogMessage':('This native value stores severity int32 at +8 and two strings at +0x10/+0x28. initWithGPULogMessage: invokes assignment helper 0x441e818 (0x443c0a8); severity is a scalar read (0x443ba88); header/message convert strings (0x443ab84, 0x443aba8).','Aggregate getter copies strings and severity (0x443c100); setter reuses native assignment (0x443c17c); destructor frees strings (0x443c188). Shared IMPs with ArcBrowserContextAttributes reflect field access/layout reuse, not shared semantic classes. No log collection backend is identified here.','Portable Arc log DTO; the GPU process log feed must be supplied separately by the host engine.','Establish severity enum, message source/order and callback delivery policy in the producer.'),
'ArcHistogramSamples':('initWithPeriodicHistogramSample: builds up to 37 ArcHistogramSample objects from present native sample fields and stores them in the 37 object slots (0x4402ad8). The individual getters are raw slot loads, many shared with unrelated classes; interpret returned object types using metadata (e.g. 0x2d0fb40, 0x31fa70).','Destructor clears the 37 slots (0x44032d8). This is a snapshot wrapper, with no collection timer, process enumeration, histogram aggregation, callback or persistence operation demonstrated in its methods. Nil represents an absent native sample branch in the initializer (0x4402ad8).','Chrome/OS metric collection lives outside the DTO. A CEF route needs an independent source for the same process-category samples; names alone do not establish measurement units or sampling intervals.','Recover sample optionality and units from the producer and ArcHistogramSample; validate all 37 constructor-source offsets against runtime samples.'),
'ArcHistoryDeletion':('The engaged native deletion payload begins at +0x10 and +8 caches the ObjC deletedItems array. Initialization copies through 0x4337338 after disposing prior state (0x442e4f4). The native flags expose all-history, expiration and time-range presence; date getters convert stored seconds (0x442e568, 0x442e57c, 0x442e590, 0x442e5a4, 0x442e5c8).','deletedItems lazily wraps ArcHistoryItem values (0x442e5ec). faviconUrls/restrictUrls build sets, and deletedVisitIds boxes native IDs (0x442e6c4, 0x442e7a8, 0x442e88c). Destruction frees native state and cached array (0x442e994). This is a deletion notification payload, not evidence that reading it deletes history.','Upstream history::DeletionInfo is a domain comparison at components/history/core/browser/history_types.h:792, not a proven direct layout mapping. Chrome history observer semantics need preservation; CEF support is not established.','Determine payload producer/notification timing, absent-range interpretation, cache validity and how restricted URLs/deleted IDs relate to actual history changes.'),
'ArcHistoryQueryOptions':('Construction allocates shared native options using 0x458d908; destruction releases the shared control block (0x4403adc, 0x43de5e8). searchText converts native UTF-16; the time setters convert NSDate seconds to Chromium-style microseconds with offset 0x295e9648864000 and saturation/NaN branches (0x44036c0, 0x4403830, 0x4403978).','maxResults reads native +0x28 (0x40cbfe8). Duplicate policy maps 0..2 and traps invalid getter state (0x4403a34); matchingAlgorithm returns zero for absent or native zero, while its setter only accepts zero/one (0x4403a74, 0x4403aa4). Upstream QueryOptions and meanings are in components/history/core/browser/history_types.h:362, :384, :398; Arc wraps additional searchText, so layout equivalence is not claimed.','A query descriptor, not an executed history query. Chrome history options provide a source-backed model; CEF route needs explicit query, dedup and time-bound behavior.','Confirm all signed enum edge cases, nil/NaN dates, default begin/end bounds and actual query consumer.'),
'ArcImportSource':('initWithImportSource: sign-extends sourceID from native int32 and translates the source type using a validity bitmask and table at 0xc9d8158, trapping unsupported values (0x4403e9c). sourceID/type are raw 64-bit slot reads at +8/+0x10 (0x2d0fb40, 0x2cb140).','This object copies two scalar values. It neither enumerates external profiles nor starts an importer, and has no declared destructor or callback. Its native ImportSource name does not establish identity with an upstream importer struct.','Portable import-source DTO, with Chrome/Safari import backends elsewhere. CEF import support cannot be concluded from this adapter.','Map each accepted native source enum to its Arc-facing value and actual importer; confirm the app-facing labels.'),
'ArcKeyEventData':('Initializer copies domCode and key strings, stores eventType at +0x10 and Windows virtual-key int32 at +8 (0x43def08). Accessors read +8/+0x10/+0x18/+0x20 (0x4081a30, 0x2cb140, 0x4084dc0, 0x4060580); destructor clears both strings (0x43defdc).','Explicit copy messages establish copy behavior for key/code in this initializer (0x43def08). No event injection, native key conversion, callback or scheduling occurs in this class. The eventType slot is scalar despite the shared Ghidra ID-return name.','Portable input-event DTO. The real keyboard dispatch path must translate it to the chosen backend and preserve physical code versus logical key.','Determine eventType enum and keyboard-layout/modifier semantics from actual consumer; do not infer from Windows key naming.'),
'ArcLoginCredentials':('Initialization stores an optional shared native credentials handle (0x443e874); aggregate getter copies it and destructor releases it (0x43df53c, 0x43df69c). url converts a native URL representation (0x443e998), username converts UTF-16 (0x443ea48).','password calls helper 0x6bd82ac and converts its returned data through the UTF-16 string helper (0x8374f3c). The helper was not followed; this does not establish secure memory, encryption or erase-on-release behavior. No keychain lookup, save or callback is demonstrated by these IMPs.','A credentials-access DTO. Chrome password-manager/keychain and CEF authentication workflows require separate investigation; the password getter does not identify the storage backend.','Recover 0x6bd82ac and credentials producer; confirm privacy/lifetime, origin matching and whether empty versus absent credentials are distinguishable.'),
'ArcMetaTagSelector':('initWithKind:value: stores a scalar kind and explicitly copies value (0x43dd458). Getters read kind at +8 and value at +0x10 (0x2d0fb40, 0x420b5f8); destructor clears the value slot (0x425b6d8).','ArcContentConversionService conversion enumerates these objects, sends kind/value and builds a native selector vector (0x43de074). This class does not query DOM metadata itself.','Portable selector DTO for the Arc conversion service; exact selector kinds and matching rules remain a service contract.','Resolve kind enum and matching case/namespace rules in the conversion backend.'),
'ArcNavigationAction':('Initializer copies native action state using 0x43452d8 (0x44084e4). url/referrer convert strings at +0x10/+0x28 (0x4408544, 0x440854c). navigationType and navigationDisposition adapt native scalar fields; disposition traps for unsupported values (0x4408554, 0x4408564).','Aggregate getter copies state via 0x4345224, setter assigns via 0x43452d8, destructor releases native string state (0x4408578, 0x440858c, 0x44085a0). This record does not itself decide navigation policy or launch a request.','Navigation callback payload can be adapted to either route, but enum mapping and the producer decision/callback timing must be preserved.','Identify the action producer and exact navigation/disposition enum names, URL/referrer normalization and any action IDs used for replies.'),
'ArcNetworkActivityMonitor':('Initialization stores an engaged shared native monitor (0x44085cc). Equality compares compatible class/native pointer and hash hashes the pointer after engagement checks (0x44086f0, 0x4408860). startLogging unwraps configuration and browser context, calls 0x432c950 and converts status through 0x4402548 (0x44088ac).','The backend rejects headless contexts and already-active logging, starts a NetExport-like writer, collects prerenderInfo/extensionInfo and schedules duration in microseconds (0x432c950). isLogging reads textual states including INITIALIZING, STARTING_LOG and LOGGING (0x4408898 → 0x432c834). This differs from stock NetExportFileWriter::IsLogging, which includes STOPPING_LOG instead of INITIALIZING (components/net_log/net_export_file_writer.cc:312).','Chrome NetExport integration is a source-backed inference from matching state strings and StartNetLog call shape (same source :157, :275). CEF logging API equivalence is unresolved; generic network interception is insufficient evidence.','Verify stop/timer callback and file finalization, the exact NetExport writer identity, thread affinity and whether overlapping monitors share a writer.'),
'ArcNetworkLoggingConfiguration':('A native file path string begins +8, with duration double at +0x20. Default init clears the path; no explicit duration store is visible in this initializer (0x443c3e4); filePath converts the native string (0x43e632c), setter converts input bytes (0x443c500), duration getter loads +0x20 (0xed0b1c).','Aggregate getter/copy setter duplicate string state (0x443c588, 0x443c5d8); destructor frees a heap string (0x440d470). It is consumed by startLogging at 0x44088ac; this class itself opens no output file.','Backend-independent logging options; duration interpretation and file lifecycle belong to the monitor backend at 0x432c950.','Confirm allocation/default duration and allowed zero/negative/nonfinite values; establish path validation and overwrite behavior in writer.'),
'ArcNotificationItem':('title and message are object slots at +8/+0x10 (0x2d0fb40, 0x2cb140). Setters replace those slots through objc store/release fixups (0x43eae2c, 0x420b588); destructor clears both (0x43dd5a4). No initializer is declared in this class.','No notification delivery, delegate, permission check or operating-system service call is present in these methods. Copy-versus-retain setter semantics require raw callsite verification because Ghidra substitutes ownership fixups.','Portable content DTO; notification platform integration resides elsewhere.','Recover setter ownership from machine code and identify producer/localization expectations.'),
'ArcRedirectEntry':('Native-copy init engages an inline record containing URL and UTF-16 title strings plus hidden and redirect-type fields (0x442cd3c). Getters require engagement; hidden is byte +0x38, redirectType int32 +0x3c (0x442ce68, 0x442ce7c).','redirect_entry copies both strings and scalar state (0x442ce90); destruction frees long strings (0x442cf28). ArcAnnotatedVisit redirectChain creates these wrappers, and setRedirectChain: converts them back (0x43ff0fc, 0x43ffb30). No redirect is executed by this record.','Portable history-chain payload, with producer semantics tied to history. No direct upstream RedirectEntry layout match is claimed.','Recover redirect-type enum and whether URL/title correspond to pre- or post-redirect entries; validate hidden handling.'),
'ArcSiteEngagementDetails':('Optional native snapshot contains a URL string at +8 and score double at +0x20; native-copy init duplicates string storage (0x442db84), URL getter converts it (0x442dc2c), score getter requires engagement (0x442dc40).','Aggregate getter copies string and score (0x442dc54); shared lifecycle IMPs clear engagement and release heap strings (0x43ed538, 0x43ed510). No engagement scoring algorithm or persistent write occurs here.','Source-backed domain comparison: components/site_engagement/content/site_engagement_score.h:29 and :148 describe upstream score state; exact backend function identity is not established. Either route needs an appropriate profile-scoped producer.','Identify site-engagement service query, score units/range and refresh semantics.'),
'ArcTabGroupProperties':('This is a partial-properties value: title, color and collapsed are independently optional. title returns nil when absent (0x443d9ec); color/collapsed box values when present (0x443dc04, 0x443dc88). Passing nil to setters clears presence; nonnil values are converted (0x443dad0, 0x443dc40, 0x443dcc4).','init initializes absent property values (0x443d8e0), native-copy init assigns through 0x441e8ec (0x443d994). Aggregate getter uses 0x5533b24; destructor frees an engaged title (0x8374f04, 0x443dd18). No group is mutated or persisted by these IMPs.','Compare upstream TabGroupVisualData at components/tab_groups/tab_group_visual_data.h:18, :35: it has concrete title/color/collapsed values, unlike this Arc partial-update payload. CEF group support needs explicit service mapping.','Confirm nil-versus-empty title and nil-versus-false collapsed behavior in the mutation consumer; map color enum.'),
'ArcURLLoadConfiguration':('A 160-byte native request config lives inline. payload string and payloadData share storage at +0x20; their setters replace that same buffer (0x440d76c, 0x440d834), so they are alternate views of one payload. URL/fileURL/string fields and headers are marshaled separately (0x440d678, 0x440d8b0, 0x440d9f8).','method maps native 1→2, 2→1, 3→3 and other values→0 using table 0xc9d8190 (0x440d71c); setter uses the same involution (0x440d744). cachePolicy normalizes to 0/1 (0x440db1c, 0x440db2c). Constructor defaults followRedirects=true, streamResponseData=false, blockLocalRequest=false and timeout=0 (0x440dd10). timeout raw instructions load d0 from +0x98 despite an empty decompiled function (0x440db0c).','This class configures a request and does not execute it. Both routes must preserve payload aliasing, headers, timeout/cache/redirect and block-local policy in their actual loader; CEF API compatibility is not proven by field names.','Identify loader consumer and enum names, local-request blocking rules, payload/file precedence, streaming callback behavior and zero timeout semantics.'),
'ArcWebContentsDevTools':('The object retains an engaged shared native DevTools handle at +0x20 and a shared delegate bridge at +0x10 (0x4414ccc, 0x4414f60). setDelegate:nil clears the bridge; a first nonnil delegate builds a bridge with weak delegate/self references, later assignments replace the stored delegate reference (0x4414f60). Destructor releases handle/bridge and cached toolbox contents (0x4415e74).','The bridge calls webContentsDevTools:displayAs:, inspectModeDidChange:, DidClose: and NeedsFocus: (0x4415fe0, 0x441604c, 0x44160b8, 0x441610c). webContents wraps the native target; toolboxWebContents caches a wrapper only while the native toolbox is available (0x44151a0, 0x4415204). execute combines domain/name/params and converts status; backend validates JSON dictionary params, joins domain.name, sends via 0x435dd94, and retains completion by request ID (0x4415520 → 0x435b114). Existing frontend opening uses DevToolsAPI.showPanel; the no-window path calls native creation at 0xc1057c0, installs a close observer and wraps toolbox state through 0x4346100 (0x4357078). Protocol connection creation has disabled/unavailable/attach-failure branches (0x4415b60 → 0x4355df8).','CEF provides overlapping CDP transport, method execution and message observation (CEF pin include/cef_browser.h:633, :649, :660) plus ShowDevTools (:582). This is a source-backed partial route, not native toolbox embedding equivalence. CEF macOS parent_view forces Alloy (include/internal/cef_types_mac.h:151); Arc toolbox/native pane behavior remains a route gate.','Verify native toolbox view ownership/display modes and callback queue; recover subscriptions, autoEnable reference counts, connection IDs and close/error ordering.'),
'ArcWebContentsMediaSession':('init:forWebContents: copies a shared native handle and stores a weak owner; destruction destroys that weak reference and releases handle/bridge/caches (0x441a1c4, 0x441b400). setDelegate: builds a shared bridge with weak delegate/owner references (0x441a4bc). position and pipController create wrapper objects from current native state, returning nil where absent (0x441b074, 0x441b254).','PiP bridge callbacks report back-to-tab/close/settings clicks and pipControllerCreated (0x441b590, 0x441b5e4, 0x441b638, 0x441b68c). Action methods forward native operations and convert status/NSError via 0x4402548. play backend rejects unavailable contents/no active session (0x441aa20 → 0x4360b58); requestPiP also rejects unsupported PiP or already-active video (0x441a6e4 → 0x436051c). Floating volume forwarding is incomplete in Ghidra output (0x441abf0).','Chromium media-session behavior is a source-backed inference against content/browser/media/session/media_session_impl.cc:704 (Resume), :739 (Suspend), :1296 (SeekTo), :1412 (SetMute). CEF SetAudioMuted at include/cef_browser.h:1003 covers a narrower host operation; it does not establish action/PiP-controller parity.','Verify seek/scrub units and errors, native volume argument, action availability, PiP ownership/auto-PiP behavior and callback sequence/thread.'),
'ArcWebContentsThumbnailsGenerator':('The wrapper has a weak owner, optional shared native generator and vector of shared observer bridges. init stores handle/weak owner, and destruction releases observers/handle and destroys the weak owner (0x441c3c0, 0x44191d8). addObserver: deduplicates by observer identity, makes weak observer/owner references, registers the bridge natively and stores it in the vector (0x441c680 → 0x436d904).','removeObserver: unregisters/removes its matching bridge (0x441c9e4 → 0x436de50). Callback 0x441cccc emits webContents:thumbnailReady: with a converted image or nil. requestThumbnail: converts backend status; 0x436df2c checks managed contents, observer/capture state and ThumbnailTabHelper availability. 0x436d69c installs a callback into thumbnail state.','Chrome ThumbnailTabHelper identity is supported by kDataKeyImpl in native calls 0x436df2c/0x436d69c and source chrome/browser/ui/thumbnails/thumbnail_tab_helper.h:27, :52; capture methods at .cc:242/:356 are source-backed candidate routes. CEF capture is not shown equivalent to this observer-driven Chrome helper lifecycle.','Recover image scale/crop/format and callback timing, no-observer request behavior, stale-image handling and visibility/capture policy.'),
'ArcWebLoginDialog':('The inline dialog value contains proxy/trust flags at +8/+9, authority UTF-16 at +0x10, and three callable objects. init copies string/callable state (0x441d2c4); setters assign that state (0x441d5cc); destruction uses 0x4346764 (0x441d734). isProxyLogin is a byte load, recovered from raw instructions despite a bad Ghidra signature (0x40b1230).','accept:with: converts nil username/password to empty native strings and invokes the callable whose entry is at +0x38, using callable storage at +0x28 (0x441d470). cancel invokes the +0x48 callable through +0x58; close separately invokes +0x68 through +0x78 (0x441d5b4, 0x441d464). No idempotence or automatic close-after-accept behavior is established. authority only converts an existing string; it does not compute trust (0x441d440).','Authentication UI can use a host callback, but three separate Arc callables and displayed security flags need matching lifetime and ordering. CEF authentication parity has not been checked here.','Trace callable producers to Chrome login handlers; determine one-shot/reentrancy, accept/cancel/close ordering, trust calculation and app presentation thread.')
}
